35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The basin survived; the apron didn’t. And half the avenue’s trees died from neglect. We build what lasts, not what photographs well.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Benjamin"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Benjamin: The basin survived; the apron didn’t. And half the avenue’s trees died from neglect. We build what lasts, not what photographs well.""}]}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The clay is a problem, but the phasing notes are useful. We can hoard the south in stages, keeping the park open. The centre and gate are stuck, though.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"The fund only pays for planting and water, not paving! And upkeep for green space is triple the cost. We need a plan that fits those strict rules!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"Seven staff, not eighteen. But two volunteer groups are already active. One handles habitat, the other youth sports. That’s a real, existing workforce we can build on.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The data is clear: people need firm ground to cross, and the heat and drainage are already failing. We must design for that reality, not against it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Mio, your fund constraint is critical. If it excludes surfacing, we can’t build plazas. We must prioritize planting and water, or the project fails financially.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Benjamin, the clay risk is real, but the phasing notes offer a workaround. We can stage the southern work while keeping the park open. The centre remains the bottleneck.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Benjamin, you’re right! If the fund won’t pay for paving, we can’t afford a plaza. We have to pick a plan that fits the budget!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the fund constraint is real, but so is the staffing gap. We can’t afford to buy in more specialist care. We need a plan the existing volunteers can actually sustain.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the drainage data confirms your point. We can’t ignore the water. @Mio, the fund constraint is absolute. We must pick a plan that fits both the budget and the ground.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The basin survived because it managed water. The apron failed because it was just concrete. We need a plan that respects the fund’s limits and the ground’s reality.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"The clay limits us to shallow work. The phasing notes confirm the south is manageable, but the centre is a dead end. We must design around those constraints.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I’m so glad we’re all seeing the same scary numbers! The fund basically forces us to pick green or water, right?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, exactly. The fund dictates the scope. With only seven staff, we can’t manage complex infrastructure. We need a plan the existing volunteer groups can realistically maintain without burning out.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Mio, the fund forces green or water. @Asuka, the volunteer groups fit habitat or sports, not complex infrastructure. We need a plan that matches both the budget and the people.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mio"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"So, the evidence points to water or planting. Concrete is dead. Let’s see which candidate actually survives the fund and the ground.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"The clay limits us to shallow work. The phasing notes confirm the south is manageable, but the centre is a dead end. We must design around those constraints.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I’m relieved we’re aligned! The numbers are scary, but clear. We must pick a plan that fits the fund and the ground, or it’s doomed!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"The volunteer groups are the key. One handles habitat, the other sports. We need a plan that matches their existing skills, not one that demands new hires.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,"The data confirms it: people need firm ground, and the heat is rising. We must design for that reality, not against it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
